691..764 Comment "/// Marks on a computation, flushed at the end. Where writes go nowhere a"
765..841 Comment "/// flushed mark leaves nothing, and where the state is kept flushing a mark"
842..916 Comment "/// keeps it. The two overlap at `flush(mark(k))` in the rows holding both"
917..993 Comment "/// `State.Eff` and `Sink`, where the rules erase marks and flushes, so both"
994..1016 Comment "/// reducts reach `k`."
